2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Emma was born Tanska farm in Järventaka village in Vesilahti, Finland where her father was a leaseholder.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her family moved to Lempäälä in 1878, and her father became the crofter of Mateuslahti croft, part of Heikkilä farm in Pyhältö village.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Lempäälä rippikirja 1875-1884 (MKO85-94)  Sivu 493 Pyhältö, Heikkilä Matheuslahti ; SSHY http://www.sukuhistoria.fi/sshy/sivut/jasenille/paikat.php?bid=14161&pnum=168 / Viitattu 08.12.2023
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Emma moved to Sääksmäki parish, to work as a servant in Liuttula "rusthåll" (large farm) in 1888. While there she gave birth to her firstborn son Kalle in 1891. After Liuttula she worked in Alivähälä farm in Vedetaka village, Sääk
2 CONC smäki, and moved back to Lempäälä in 1898, working in Pietilä farm in Sarvikas village.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married croft farmer Emil Vilhelm of Suoniemi, 7 years her junior, in 1899, and had 5 more children with him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emma became a widow when Emil died in 1918.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
