1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Linda Salonen Obituary
2 CONT Mrs. Linda Helena Salonen, 89 years, of Nipigon, Ontario passed away peacefully on Tuesday, January 12, 2010, at her residence at the Nipigon District Memorial Hospital. Born in Tampere, Finland, Linda came to Nemeges, Ontario (he
2 CONC r dad worked for the C.P.R. ) in 1923, with her family. She moved to Nipigon in 1936 and lived with her aunt and uncle - Elsa and Eino Jokinen. Over the years Linda worked for the Co Op Store, Nick Salo's Store, L & L Food Market 
2 CONC for nine years and retired from The Bay in 1981 after seventeen years. She married Bert Salonen in 1940 and lived on the west coast for two years between 1941 and 1944 while Bert was in the army. Linda's main interests were bowlin
2 CONC g and curling in her earlier years, BINGO, playing Rummoli with her friends, fishing with the family, summers spent at their cottage at Lofquist Lake and while Bert was living, winters spent in Florida. Linda was a life member of 
2 CONC the Royal Purple #141, Nipigon, a member of the Silver Club, of the Nipigon Lioness and of the Nipigon Hospital Auxiliary. Predeceased by her husband Bert in 1989, by her parents - Elna and Kalle Lehtinen, by her step-mother Lydia
2 CONC  Lehtinen, by her brother Matti and his wife Florence Lehtinen, by her sister Anne and her husband Kusti Kolppanen, by her sister-in-law and brother-in-law - Laila and Mike Makkne, by her cousin Ann and her husband Vic Koskela, an
2 CONC d by her son-in-law Gordon Dyck; she is survived by her daughter Diana Dyck of Nipigon, niece Anita MacDonald of Thunder Bay, Ontario, by three godchildren as well as numerous nieces and nephews in Canada and Finland. Resting at t
2 CONC he Elliott Funeral Home Ltd. , Nipigon where friends may call from 4 P.M. until 7:30 P.M. on Thursday, January 14, 2010. The Ladies of the Royal Purple #141, Nipigon will be holding a memorial service at the funeral home on Thursd
2 CONC ay evening at 7 P.M. Funeral services for Linda Salonen will be held on Friday, January 15, 2010 at 11 A.M. at Grace United Church, Nipigon with Roberta Beyer R. -D.L.M. officiating. Interment will be in Cliffside Cemetery, Nipigo
2 CONC n. Friends so wishing may make donations to the Nipigon District Memorial Hospital Long Term Care."
2 CONT
2 CONT Published by The Thunder Bay Chronicle Journal on Jan. 14, 2010.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
